From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] unit: test the atoms that queue D-Bus requests

Builds the real network, radio-settings, sms and call-forwarding atoms on
a small model of the modem, with scripted drivers that finish an
operation when the test says so, and calls them from a second bus
connection. For each atom: a second client gets an answer and not
InProgress, requests that can share one driver call do, a failure reaches
the right requests, nothing is answered twice, and what waits when the
atom goes away is answered, also when the driver answers from remove().

Runs under dbus-run-session; without a bus it reports itself skipped.
test-dbus.c now allows a test without a start callback.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending

